{"id": "EUVD-2026-103621", "enisaUuid": "28a084d3-4c3a-37ad-97dc-d7afdcc9e999", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfc: llcp: fix slab-out-of-bounds reads when logging service names\n\nnfc_llcp_wks_sap() and nfc_llcp_build_sdreq_tlv() pass non-null-\nterminated strings to pr_debug() using the %s format specifier.\nThe buffers are allocated via kmemdup() or come from netlink\nattributes and are not guaranteed to be null-terminated, causing\n__dynamic_pr_debug() to read beyond the allocated region:\n\n  KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds Read in __dynamic_pr_debug\n\nFix both call sites by using %.*s with the explicit length to limit\nthe output to the actual length of the string.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:01", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/75f7c5a42fa1483f5912279a749417c284ad708f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6d4ca872830e46fcca9c086bf19fa9bd2faf09d2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a143f7835faa4fe0178448289feea4f84eeee8d6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/75bfd9ef4da2fb49dac1f19880d2ac4ccd07b45b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8afb6c194f5781798d3ab3edf243cf5a24a9d1f9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8978dff632519712d1fa432991e1f2e857f90239", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4262b12277a3e056c95fc49e9c4d7bd97035d16c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7dcf371a35632f035baf77bcf2c129165f772ce4"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4wv6-7jcw-864j", "CVE-2026-98576"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "13de3af8-a7fd-3d8c-a585-248afb9c552f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "1f49877e-591b-3ac9-bf01-35f85bc13b7e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d9b8d8e19b073096d3609bbd60f82148d128b555 <8afb6c194f5781798d3ab3edf243cf5a24a9d1f9"}, {"id": "2429e964-c2ca-3fd1-a7a1-70a836e648fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor